I think the reason "sequence" is used in the docstring type parameters section instead of array-like is because we don't accept zero or multi dimension arrays. see #41807 for discussion.

see also #32773, https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/32773#issuecomment-600064248, https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/32773#issuecomment-840216855 and #32033 for discussions relating to avoiding the numpydoc type definitions for internal docstrings to therefore avoid the discrepancies (not relevant here as the base class docstrings are our api definitions for 3rd party EA developers)

if we could sometime in the future use the standard type notation in the public dosctrings that would be great (and redundant)
